# Orchestration Playbook

Status: live
Last verified: {{DATE}}

## Start

1. Read live git/worktree state and the relevant authority docs; do not fetch during a read-only audit.
2. Put every delegated task in the six-part Agent slice issue/template with `Completion tier`.
3. Give each editing agent an isolated fetched-base worktree; reviewers are read-only and forbid every
   tree-mutating git command.
4. Use Agent View (`claude agents`) for concurrent session status and the goal/evaluator templates for exits.

## Saved drift workflow

Enter Claude plan mode first, then invoke `orchestration-drift-audit`. Plan mode is the permission boundary;
prompt language alone is not a tool-permission boundary; the workflow's read-only wording is defense-in-depth.
It reports only evidence-backed
repo/GitHub/control discrepancies and never edits.

## Action authority

`{{ACTION_AUTHORITY_PATH}}` is the single machine-readable authority. In-scope branch/worktree creation,
commit, and draft/ready PR creation/update are autonomous. Push is conditional on live proof that it cannot
trigger a preview/production deploy, publish or billed build, production write, or external contact; a preview
counts as a deploy and uncertainty falls back to human approval. PR merge is conditional: every listed
condition must be proven, including no deploy or production effect; uncertainty falls back to human approval.

Production-affecting push, deploy/publish, production mutation or configuration, data migrations, destructive/irreversible actions,
billed actions or purchases, external contact, secrets, and unresolved product/design/material-architecture
decisions remain human-gated. A merge that auto-deploys or otherwise mutates production is human-gated.

Required merge/release gates remain indivisible and green, but closure means zero verified release blockers,
not zero findings. Treat unknown/unverified, release/core-journey, security/tenancy/privacy, compliance,
data-integrity, irreversible/external/billed, and proof-trust defects as BLOCK. A residual is FIX-NEXT only
when evidence proves it bounded, fail-safe, and unable to affect any BLOCK class. File FIX-NEXT evidence,
impact, owner, fix direction, and validation in the durable backlog before merge, then repair it on a
follow-up branch. A red mandatory gate cannot be downgraded; fix the product or a proven-stale gate and rerun.
Unknown is never low severity.

## Functionality-first delivery loop

For functional code changes (product behavior and controls/gates): root cause + current provider/contract
truth → exact biting tests as targeted implementation proof → proportional deploy-safety proof
(migration/schema, DB integrity, build/startup, deploy readiness only) → human-authorized merge/deploy +
**deployed functional proof** of the original user journey → remediate queued findings and run the broad
closure gate on the hardened candidate. The motive is efficiency: prove the intended behavior — ideally on
the real surface — before any time/tokens go to hardening, broad audits, cleanup, or edge-polish. Auditors
may inspect in parallel before acceptance, but findings remain queue-only unless they identify a bounded
interruption class in `.ai-organization/policies/delivery-lifecycle.v1.json`. Docs, mocks, and planning
are exempt from the staged lifecycle. Never let review ceremony substitute for proving the feature works
on the deployed artifact.

## Evidence

Open real outputs/artifacts. A status, report, grep-zero, green test, or critic verdict is a lead. Re-run
surprising results a second way and record every not-reached surface.
